# File-size baseline for the core workspace (VRS04, check-file-size.sh).
# Reconciled 2026-07-13 to current reality: 17 stale entries dropped
# (files split below threshold or removed). Only currently-oversized
# files are grandfathered here.
#
# Entry form:  <relative_path> <count>   or   <relative_path> exempt
#   <count>  numbered ratchet: fails only if the file grows past the
#            next 100-line ceiling above <count> (slack, not +1 line).
#            Bump the number when a growth is legitimate.
#   exempt   structurally un-splittable (FFI facade, migration ledger,
#            protocol state machine): never fails. There is no split the
#            failure could prompt, so a running line count buys nothing.
#
# Splitting rules + the exempt categories: _private/.claude/rules/file-size.md.
# SPLIT-phase tracking for the numbered entries below: PRB-2026-032.
# Suppression alternative: "// allow(large_file)" on line 1 of a file.

